## WHAT n8n IS

n8n is a workflow automation platform. A workflow is a graph of nodes connected by edges. Each node is an integration (HTTP Request, GitHub, Qdrant, Anthropic, etc.) or a logic operator (If, Switch, Merge, Loop, Code). Workflows are triggered by Trigger nodes (Webhook, Schedule, n8n Trigger, etc.) and execute nodes in sequence.

Key operational facts:
  - New workflows are always created INACTIVE. Activation must be explicit (PUT /workflows/:id/activate).
  - Updating an active workflow via PUT automatically re-activates with the new definition.
  - CLI update:workflow modifies the database directly — changes don't take effect until n8n restarts.
  - Workflow names are limited to 128 characters (critical when migrating from SQLite to Postgres).
  - The public REST API requires a paid plan for n8n Cloud (not available during free trial).
  - Self-hosted n8n has the API available at /api/v1/ on the same host as the UI.

