## API FUNDAMENTALS

### Base URL
  https://{{N8N_HOST}}/api/v1/

### Authentication
  Header: X-N8N-API-KEY: {{N8N_API_KEY}}

  Generate the key: Settings → n8n API → Create API Key
  The key is shown ONCE. Store it securely immediately.
  All endpoints require this header — there is no session-based auth for the API.

### Standard request pattern
  curl -s \
    -H "X-N8N-API-KEY: {{N8N_API_KEY}}" \
    -H "Accept: application/json" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    https://{{N8N_HOST}}/api/v1/<path>

### Pagination
  All list endpoints use cursor-based pagination.
  Default page size: 100. Maximum: 250.

  Request next page:
    ?limit=100&cursor=<nextCursor_value>

  Response includes nextCursor when more pages exist:
  {
    "data": [...],
    "nextCursor": "eyJ..."   // absent or null when on the last page
  }

  Pagination loop pattern:
    1. Request with ?limit=250
    2. If response.nextCursor exists → request again with ?cursor=<value>
    3. Stop when nextCursor is absent or null

