## ENDPOINT REFERENCE

### Workflows
  GET    /api/v1/workflows                    — List workflows
         ?active=true|false                  — Filter by active state
         ?tags=tag1,tag2                     — Filter by tags
         ?limit=100&cursor=...               — Pagination
  POST   /api/v1/workflows                    — Create workflow (always created INACTIVE)
  GET    /api/v1/workflows/{id}               — Get workflow by ID
  PUT    /api/v1/workflows/{id}               — Update workflow (auto-reactivates if was active)
  DELETE /api/v1/workflows/{id}               — Delete workflow ⚠ (must archive first, or use force)
  POST   /api/v1/workflows/{id}/activate      — Activate (publish) workflow — makes triggers live
  POST   /api/v1/workflows/{id}/deactivate    — Deactivate workflow — stops triggers
  POST   /api/v1/workflows/{id}/run           — Trigger workflow execution via API
         ⚠ Does NOT support passing input data. Use Webhook node for data-driven triggers.
  GET    /api/v1/workflows/{id}/tags          — Get workflow tags
  PUT    /api/v1/workflows/{id}/tags          — Update workflow tags
         body: [{"id": "tag-uuid-1"}, {"id": "tag-uuid-2"}]
  GET    /api/v1/workflows/{id}/history       — Get workflow version history
  GET    /api/v1/workflows/{id}/history/{versionId} — Get a specific historical version

  Workflow object fields of note:
    id         — numeric string ID (used in API paths and webhook URLs)
    name       — display name (≤128 chars)
    active     — bool: is the workflow live?
    tags       — array of {id, name} objects
    createdAt  — ISO-8601
    updatedAt  — ISO-8601
    nodes      — array of node definitions
    connections — node wiring

### Executions
  GET    /api/v1/executions                   — List executions
         ?status=success|error|waiting|running|canceled
         ?workflowId=<id>                     — Filter by workflow
         ?includeData=true                    — Include full node data (expensive)
         ?limit=100&cursor=...
  GET    /api/v1/executions/{id}              — Get single execution + full data
  DELETE /api/v1/executions/{id}              — Delete execution record
  POST   /api/v1/executions/{id}/retry        — Retry a failed/stopped execution
         body: {"loadWorkflow": true}         — true = retry with latest workflow version
                                              — false/omit = retry with snapshot from original run

  Execution object fields of note:
    id         — numeric execution ID
    finished   — bool: has it completed?
    mode       — "manual" | "trigger" | "webhook" | "retry" | "cli"
    startedAt  — ISO-8601
    stoppedAt  — ISO-8601 (null if still running)
    workflowId — ID of the workflow that ran
    status     — "success" | "error" | "waiting" | "running" | "canceled"
    data.resultData.runData — per-node input/output data (when includeData=true)
    data.resultData.error   — error message and stack on failed executions

### Credentials
  GET    /api/v1/credentials                  — List credentials (metadata only, no secret values)
         ?type=httpHeaderAuth&limit=100
  POST   /api/v1/credentials                  — Create credential
  GET    /api/v1/credentials/{id}             — Get credential metadata
  PUT    /api/v1/credentials/{id}             — Update credential
  DELETE /api/v1/credentials/{id}             — Delete credential
  GET    /api/v1/credentials/schema/{credentialTypeName} — Get the data schema for a credential type

  ⚠ Credentials API NEVER returns secret values (passwords, API keys, tokens).
    It returns metadata: type, name, id, createdAt — not the credential data itself.
    Credential data is encrypted in the n8n database at all times.

  Credential type names (common):
    httpHeaderAuth       — API key in header
    httpBasicAuth        — Basic auth
    httpBearerAuth       — Bearer token
    oAuth2Api            — OAuth2
    anthropicApi         — Anthropic Claude
    openAiApi            — OpenAI
    githubApi            — GitHub
    qdrantApi            — Qdrant
    postgresDb           — PostgreSQL
    redisDb              — Redis

### Tags
  GET    /api/v1/tags                         — List all tags
  POST   /api/v1/tags                         — Create tag
         body: {"name": "production"}
  GET    /api/v1/tags/{id}                    — Get tag
  PUT    /api/v1/tags/{id}                    — Update tag name
  DELETE /api/v1/tags/{id}                    — Delete tag

  Tags are global — visible and usable across all users/projects.
  Establish a naming convention early: prod, staging, fabric, aiana, cve, linkedin, etc.

### Variables
  GET    /api/v1/variables                    — List variables
  POST   /api/v1/variables                    — Create variable
