## WEBHOOK TRIGGERING (the right way to pass data)

The REST API /run endpoint does NOT support custom input data. For data-driven workflow invocation, use the Webhook node:

  Webhook URLs:
    Test (editor open):       https://{{N8N_HOST}}/webhook-test/<path>
    Production (activated):   https://{{N8N_HOST}}/webhook/<path>

  ⚠ /webhook-test/ ONLY works while the n8n editor is open and listening.
    Always use /webhook/ against an activated workflow in production.

  Example: trigger a fabric workflow with payload
    curl -X POST https://{{N8N_HOST}}/webhook/fabric-alert \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer {{WEBHOOK_AUTH_TOKEN}}" \
      -d '{"source": "sandfly", "alert_id": "abc123", "severity": 4}'

  Response mode options (set on Webhook node):
    "On Last Node Completion" — waits for workflow to complete, returns last node output
    "Immediately"             — returns 200 OK right away, workflow runs async
    "Using 'Respond to Webhook' Node" — returns whatever the Respond node sends

  For workflows > 10 seconds, use "Immediately" to avoid HTTP timeouts.

  Webhook auth options (set on Webhook node):
    None — public webhook (fine for internal network)
    Basic Auth — username + password
    Header Auth — custom header name + value (recommended)

