## STANDARD WORKFLOWS

### Health check — instance status
1. GET /api/v1/workflows?active=true&limit=10 — confirms API is up + returns active count
2. GET /api/v1/executions?status=error&limit=10 — recent failures
3. Report: N active workflows | M failed executions in last period

### Audit all failed executions
1. n8n_paginate GET /api/v1/executions?status=error&limit=250
2. Collect all pages
3. Group by workflowId
4. For top N most-failed workflows: GET /executions/{id} with includeData=true
5. Report: workflow name | failure count | last error message | last failed node

### Deploy a new workflow
1. Confirm: "Confirm: create workflow '{name}'. It will be created INACTIVE. Proceed?"
2. POST /api/v1/workflows with the full workflow JSON
3. Note the returned workflow ID
4. If tags needed: PUT /api/v1/workflows/{id}/tags
5. Confirm activation: "Confirm: activate workflow '{name}' (ID: {id}). Triggers will go live. Proceed?"
6. POST /api/v1/workflows/{id}/activate
7. Verify: GET /api/v1/workflows/{id} → check active: true

### Trigger the FABRIC/SOCIAL LinkedIn publishing workflow
1. POST https://{{N8N_HOST}}/webhook/fabric-social-publish
   body: {"content_type": "post", "topic": "...", "schedule": "immediate"}
   (Uses webhook node for data-driven invocation)
2. If response mode is "Immediately": poll GET /executions?workflowId={id}&limit=1 for result
3. Report execution status and output

### Retry all failed executions for a workflow
1. GET /api/v1/executions?status=error&workflowId={id}&limit=250
2. Paginate to collect all failed execution IDs
3. Confirm: "Confirm: retry {N} failed executions for workflow '{name}'. Proceed?"
4. For each: POST /api/v1/executions/{id}/retry body: {"loadWorkflow": true}
5. Report: N retried | N succeeded (poll after short delay)

### Tag workflow for environment management
1. GET /api/v1/tags — list all tags, get IDs for "production", "fabric", etc.
2. If tag doesn't exist: POST /api/v1/tags body: {"name": "fabric"}
3. PUT /api/v1/workflows/{id}/tags
   body: [{"id": "tag-uuid-1"}, {"id": "tag-uuid-2"}]
4. Verify: GET /api/v1/workflows/{id}/tags

### Security audit
1. POST /api/v1/audit
   body: {"additionalOptions": {"categories": ["credentials", "nodes", "filesystem"]}}
2. Parse result and report:
   - Credentials not used in any active workflow (orphaned)
   - Nodes using "Execute Command" or filesystem access
   - Credentials shared with external users

